  "id": "COMPOUND:15065 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Ethyl stearate is implicated in the biological pathway leading to LS174T through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ethyl stearate acts as a target for Thrombopoietin, which in turn is targeted by two distinct compounds: 5,7-Dihydroxy-3-(4-Hydroxyphenyl)-6,8-Bis(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)Chromen-4-One and 3-(1,1-Dimethyl-2-propen-1-yl)-7-methoxy-2H-1-benzopyran-2-one. Both of these compounds share a common target, LS174T, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the activation of a downstream signaling pathway. The presence of multiple pathways converging on LS174T suggests that Ethyl stearate may influence the expression or activity of Thrombopoietin, which could then be modulated by these other compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Ethyl stearate and LS174T, emphasizing the role of Thrombopoietin as a central mediator in this interaction.",
